rally if first interval has start >= end? invalid. But for valid intervals start <= end, first won't append unless start == end? Actually if [3,3], 3<3 false, append duplicate. But bug is redundant processing first interval; should iterate intervals[1:]. Also if sort by start, first interval may be [3,3], duplicate. So bug: loop should start at intervals[1:] to avoid reprocessing first interval.\n3 Overlap condition uses current[0] < last[1], but touching intervals like [1,3] and [3,5] should be merged? User says test cases including touching intervals like [1,3] and [3,5]. Usually merge overlapping intervals may consider touching as overlapping if end == start? The prompt says merge overlapping intervals and return sorted by start; test cases including touching intervals like [1,3] and", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0007565498235635459], [22916, -8.194622993469238]], [[1144, -1.3113108252582606e-05], [513, -12.107057571411133]], [[4087, -0.006935091223567724], [5707, -5.063690185546875]], [[1156, -0.0032998467795550823], [303, -5.828987121582031]], [[579, -0.9155269265174866], [13, -1.2635265588760376]], [[1622, -0.023821206763386726], [3296, -4.167490482330322]], [[13, -0.0285560991615057], [25, -3.7678921222686768]], [[14235, -0.1091068834066391], [26472, -3.3229494094848633]], [[1423, -0.8895934820175171], [10229, -1.5180381536483765]], [[21851, -0.46372854709625244], [1396, -1.0441651344299316]], [[303, -0.21753129363059998], [11, -1.6850128173828125]], [[12654, -0.23877063393592834], [2574, -2.199465751647949]], [[709, -0.22681798040866852], [10562, -1.6081923246383667]], [[11, -1.0139135122299194], [10562, -1.0822957754135132]], [[10033, -0.0030401020776480436], [1754, -6.418694972991943]], [[1754, -0.003636287758126855], [799, -5.668299674987793]], [[799, -0.6939330697059631], [303, -0.705844521522522]], [[303, -0.06896214932203293], [799, -3.0047264099121094]], [[799, -3.695494797284482e-06], [11316, -13.590412139892578]], [[11316, -9.179157132166438e-06], [3106, -1